# of an OrderedMap live in the storage of a PRIVATE inner map. `insert` on the
# outer object mutates only `self._map`, another object, so the inner map's own
# entry assert would check the wrong flag. The per-parameter mask records that
# `insert` mutates storage reachable THROUGH `self` (a deep bit), so the outer
# object carries the assert and panics under a live borrow of its entries.
